  "en": {
    "title": "Why the sky is blue – Plümo and the paint roller",
    "hooks": [
      {"type": "misconception", "spoken": "Nobody painted the sky blue. I checked. With a paint roller.",
       "on_screen": "Nobody *painted* the sky.", "scores": {"clarity": 5, "relevance": 4, "curiosity": 5, "truth": 5, "visual": 5},
       "source_ids": ["S1", "S2"], "visual": "paint roller flies to the Fact Door, stamp NOPE",
       "why": {"truth": "NASA and Met Office: blue comes from sunlight scattered by the air", "visual": "paint roller at the door reads at once"}},
      {"type": "question", "spoken": "Why is the sky blue and not purple?", "on_screen": "Why not *purple*?",
       "scores": {"clarity": 4, "relevance": 4, "curiosity": 5, "truth": 5, "visual": 3}, "source_ids": ["S2"], "visual": "sky flashes purple"},
      {"type": "surprising_fact", "spoken": "Violet light gets scattered even more than blue.", "on_screen": "Violet scatters *more*.",
       "scores": {"clarity": 3, "relevance": 3, "curiosity": 4, "truth": 5, "visual": 3}, "source_ids": ["S2"], "visual": "violet bar above blue"},
      {"type": "concrete_risk", "spoken": "Say the sky is just dyed blue at a quiz night and you lose the point.", "on_screen": "Dyed blue? *Point lost.*",
       "scores": {"clarity": 4, "relevance": 3, "curiosity": 3, "truth": 4, "visual": 2}, "source_ids": ["S1"], "visual": "quiz card"},
      {"type": "demonstration", "spoken": "I hold my paint roller up to the sky. Watch.", "on_screen": "Paint roller vs *sky*.",
       "scores": {"clarity": 4, "relevance": 3, "curiosity": 4, "truth": 4, "visual": 5}, "source_ids": [], "visual": "Plümo with paint roller"}
    ],
    "beats": [
      {"function": "hook", "scene_type": "zonk_scan", "source_ids": ["S1", "S2"],
       "spoken": "Nobody painted the sky blue. I checked. With a paint roller.",
       "data": {"mode": "hook", "head": "Nobody *painted* the sky.", "head_at": 0.2, "sign": "FACTS ONLY",
                "items": [{"kind": "paint_roller"}], "stamp_reject": "NOPE",
                "cue_scan": "sky", "cue_verdict": "painted", "cue_club": "checked", "cue_know": "roller"}},
      {"function": "problem", "scene_type": "zonk_word", "source_ids": ["S1"],
       "spoken": "Wait. I thought somebody painted it up there. But there is no paint. Just air and sunlight. I was shocked. I had already bought a roller. Fluffy.",
       "data": {"word_a": "Blue", "word_b": "paint", "left": "Plümo: *blue paint*", "right": "Real: *air + light*",
                "cue_left": "thought", "cue_strike": "no", "cue_right": "air", "cue_react": "I",
                "item": "paint_roller", "cue_shock": "shocked", "cue_item": "roller", "cue_never": "Fluffy"}},
      {"function": "explanation", "scene_type": "zonk_diagram", "source_ids": ["S1"],
       "spoken": "So what happens? Sunlight hits the gases and particles in the air. They scatter the light in all directions. And blue gets scattered more than the other colors. No hands, so I point with my leaf.",
       "data": {"headline": "What does the *air* do?", "inner": "sun", "disc": ["#1F5FD8", "#BFE4FF", "#5FA8F0"], "cue_q": "air",
                "labels": [{"text": "gases and *particles*", "pos": "tr", "cue": "gases"},
                           {"text": "scatter *everywhere*", "pos": "l", "cue": "scatter"},
                           {"text": "blue: scattered *more*", "pos": "b", "cue": "blue"}],
                "cue_hands": "hands", "cue_leaf": "leaf"},
       "overlay": {"marker_at": "w:gases"}},
      {"function": "demonstration", "scene_type": "zonk_zoom", "source_ids": ["S1", "S2"],
       "spoken": "Closer. Blue light travels in shorter, smaller waves. Red light in longer ones. The gases scatter short waves much more. Scientists call it Rayleigh scattering. Sounds like a sneeze. Bless you.",
       "data": {"kind": "sky_blue", "lens": "wave_blue", "lens_bg": "#101830", "cue_mag": "Closer",
                "callouts": [{"text": "Blue: *short* waves", "cue": "Blue"}, {"text": "Red: *long* waves", "cue": "Red"}],
                "cue_nut": "smaller", "stamp": {"text": "Rayleigh!", "cue": "Rayleigh"}, "cue_react": "sneeze", "cue_fast": "Bless"},
       "overlay": {"dim_at": "w:Blue", "marker_at": "w:Blue"}},
      {"function": "insight", "scene_type": "zonk_compare", "source_ids": ["S2"],
       "spoken": "Red gets scattered less, blue a lot more, and violet even more. So why isn't the sky purple? Our eyes respond more strongly to blue, and sunlight has less violet in it. I squinted purple anyway.",
       "data": {"headline": "Why not *purple*?",
                "bars": [{"label": "Red", "value": "less", "h": 0.3, "color": "#FF4D4D", "cue": "Red"},
                         {"label": "Blue", "value": "a lot", "h": 0.75, "color": "#4D7CFF", "cue": "blue"},
                         {"label": "Violet", "value": "even more", "h": 0.95, "color": "#A97BFF", "cue": "violet"}],
                "stamp": {"text": "Eyes: blue!", "cue": "eyes"}, "cue_react": "squinted"},
       "overlay": {"marker_at": "w:Red"}},
      {"function": "benefit", "scene_type": "zonk_scan",
       "spoken": "Remember: the sky isn't painted. The air scatters the blue our way. My turn. Scanner on. Result: color unknown. I guess I'm green.",
       "data": {"mode": "unknown", "sign": "FACTS ONLY", "merke": "The sky is *scattered light*, not paint.",
                "display": "Color: unknown", "plumps": "FLOP", "cue_build": "scatters",
                "cue_go": "My", "cue_scan": "Scanner", "cue_result": "Result", "cue_back": "guess"},
       "overlay": {"marker_at": "w:Remember"}},
      {"function": "close", "scene_type": "zonk_loop",
       "spoken": "I'll just lie here for a bit. More Zonkfruit? Follow the channel. I'll get up in a minute.",
       "data": {"sign": "FACTS ONLY", "cta": "More Zonkfruit? *Follow.*", "cue_cta": "More", "cue_up": "get", "cue_lie": "lie", "cue_ch": "channel"}}
    ],
